      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `extract_text.py` file that extracts plain text from a scanned document image using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful OCR (Optical Character Recognition) service provided by AWS. The integration will be identifiable by the import of the `boto3` library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, and the use of the `textract` client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864573471,
          "start": 1789864571464
        },
        "type": "text"
